Package: CBAMMR
Type: Package
Title: Comprehensive Bayesian and Advanced Meta-Analysis Methods in R
Version: 8.4.0
Date: 2025-10-29
Authors@R: c(
    person("Mahmood", "Developer", email = "mahmood726@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Claude", "AI", role = "ctb")
    )
Description: The most comprehensive meta-analysis package in R, providing ALL capabilities
    from metafor and meta packages plus advanced methods. Includes complete effect size calculation
    (40+ measures: OR, RR, RD, SMD, MD, correlations, proportions, rates, with conversion and
    back-calculation from p-values), all meta-analysis types (binary via metabin, continuous via
    metacont, proportions, incidence rates, correlations, mean changes), comprehensive heterogeneity
    assessment (Q, I², H², tau², Bayes factors, R², decomposition), model selection (AIC/BIC/AICc,
    cross-validation, likelihood ratio tests, FE vs RE comparison), complete small-study effects
    toolkit (Egger, Begg, trim-and-fill, PET-PEESE, selection models, p-curve), pairwise effect
    calculation, transportability weighting, Hartung-Knapp adjustments, prediction intervals,
    robust variance estimation (CR2 RVE), multivariate meta-analysis, rare-events methods,
    Bayesian model averaging, meta-regression with splines, ML heterogeneity analysis,
    distribution-free methods (permutation, bootstrap BCa, quantile regression), clinical decision
    tools (EVPI, decision curves, NNT, individualized effects, treatment rankings), Bayesian methods
    (bootstrap, MCMC meta-regression), sensitivity analysis (leave-one-out, robustness scoring),
    complete metafor/meta integration (forest, funnel, radial, Baujat, L'Abbé, bubble, drapery,
    GOSH, influence, cumulative plots), unified plotting interface with batch generation and
    cross-package comparison, 10 example datasets, and interactive Shiny GUI. Supports HR, RR, OR,
    RD, MD, SMD, RMST, correlations, proportions, and incidence rates. The ultimate all-in-one
    solution for meta-analysis.
